From b92d863e5c38a25ba971cd6ba6a5030199365e41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:00:41 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(skills): project skills and global skills

skill_manage takes a scope ('project' or 'global'). A plugin that knows a chat's project registers a provider (agent.skill_utils.register_project_skills_provider); that project's skills dir is then a project root for the chat and its subagents: listed, loaded and edited only there, marked project, winning over a global skill of the same name, without a trust entry or scan. In a chat with a project a create must name its scope; a global skill that names the project gets a warning. The tool description, SKILLS_GUIDANCE and the memory tool description say where each kind of knowledge goes. Without a provider nothing changes.
